so obviously there are tons and tons of  protons in the Sun the question is if  the Sun were totally made of protons  how many would there be well we can work  that out by taking the total mass of the  Sun 2 times 10 to the 30 kilograms and  dividing by the mass of one proton which  is 1 point 6 7 3 times 10 to the minus  27 kilograms and the answer you'll find  is 1.19 5 times 10 to the power of 57  protons if the Sun were totally made of  protons that is how many would be there  that's really an unthinkable number it's  basically a 1 followed by 50 seven  zeroes a huge number of protons now if  you don't have a calculator handy you  can actually solve this kind of problem  by typing it straight into the Google  search field what you need to do is put  in to e 30 now Google interprets this e  as times 10 to the then divided by 1  point 6 7 3 e - minus 27 so if you type  that straight into the Google search  field you will find it'll give you the  answer 1 point 1 9 5 times 10 to the  power of 57
 

